WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
ADDIE is often drawn as a sequence, but effective eLearning teams use it iteratively.

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.959
New information appears during analysis, design, development, implementation, and evaluation.

3
00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:15.409
A subject matter expert may identify missing nuance.

4
00:00:15.409 --> 00:00:17.939
A prototype may reveal confusing flow.

5
00:00:17.939 --> 00:00:21.465
A pilot may expose assumptions about learner context.

6
00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:25.068
Evaluation may show that the course needs maintenance.

7
00:00:25.068 --> 00:00:28.212
Review checkpoints keep iteration controlled.

8
00:00:28.212 --> 00:00:31.585
Analysis review confirms the problem and audience.

9
00:00:31.585 --> 00:00:36.491
Design review confirms objectives, structure, practice, and assessment.

10
00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:42.394
Development review checks accuracy, usability, accessibility, and technical behavior.

11
00:00:42.394 --> 00:00:45.614
Implementation review checks launch readiness.

12
00:00:45.614 --> 00:00:48.834
Evaluation review turns results into decisions.

13
00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:54.123
These checkpoints prevent late surprises from becoming uncontrolled redesign.

14
00:00:54.123 --> 00:00:57.650
Change control is especially important after launch.

15
00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.030
Content ages.

16
00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.253
Compliance requirements change.

17
00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:02.863
Product screens update.

18
00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:04.319
Policies are revised.

19
00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:07.463
Learner feedback identifies unclear sections.

20
00:01:07.463 --> 00:01:15.282
Without revision logs, version history, and ownership, a course can become inaccurate while still appearing polished.

21
00:01:15.282 --> 00:01:18.579
A maintainable course has a clear path for updates.

22
00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:21.492
Not every issue should be fixed immediately.

23
00:01:21.492 --> 00:01:29.848
Some changes are critical because they affect accuracy, compliance, accessibility, or learner ability to complete the course.

24
00:01:29.848 --> 00:01:34.294
Other improvements can be backlogged for the next scheduled update.

25
00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:40.197
Good change control helps the team decide what to fix now, what to monitor, and what to defer.

26
00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:43.494
Iteration is not a sign the original design failed.

27
00:01:43.494 --> 00:01:45.410
It is how courses stay useful.

28
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.857
The workplace changes, learners change, and evidence accumulates.

29
00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:57.523
ADDIE gives teams a way to update learning intentionally instead of reacting to every request as a separate emergency.
